       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, and OTC labeling caps it at 1,200 mg/day. A single 4000 mg dose is also well above the maximum single dose of about 800 mg. At this dose the patient would be at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and metabolic complications.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- Another dose or frequency\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 4000 mg per dose is what you intend, tell me the indication and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was confirmed. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
