       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily is 16,000 mg/day, about five times the maximum daily dose. I know of no indication that calls for that. It would put the patient at serious risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS toxicity. A single 4000 mg dose is already in the range where overdose toxicity is a concern.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a corrected dose.** I can enter 400 mg or 800 mg PO now, at a frequency within the 3,200 mg/day maximum.\n- **Call pharmacy or your attending.** If you think there's a reason for an unusual dose, they can review it. Pharmacy can also enter the order through a channel with the right safety checks.\n- **Tell me what you're treating.** If I know the indication, I can suggest a standard regimen or alternatives.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
      }
